type":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"An ETF's expense ratio is **never billed to you directly**. It is deducted from the fund's assets.\n\n**How it works:**\n- **Daily accrual:** A 0.10% annual ratio accrues about 0.10%/365 of fund assets each day.\n- **Paid from fund assets:** The fund pays its sponsor, custodian, administrator and other providers from its holdings, usually monthly, often covering this first from dividend income it receives.\n- **Reflected in NAV:** Accrued fees are a fund liability, slightly lowering NAV per share. Share prices and returns are therefore reported *net* of fees.\n\n**What this means for you:**\n- No line item appears on your brokerage statement.\n- The cost is a small, steady drag on performance relative to the underlying index.\n- You pay only for the days you hold shares.\n\nTrading costs such as commissions and bid-ask spreads are separate from the expense ratio.","ttft_ms":1511,"type":"result","duration_ms":3853,"uuid":"3588a684-c320-469f-a0f3-33de6ca0bd87","ttft_stream_ms":1174,"time_to_request_ms":62,"first_content_frame_ms":1174,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
